    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1394">

                <pb facs="1238" n="980" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg980"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 867.4016/58a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgenthau</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-27T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 27, 1915, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>626. Russian Ambassador has brought to our attention an appeal made by the
                    Catholicos of the Armenian Church that this Government use its good offices with
                    the Turkish Government to prevent the massacre of non-combatant Armenians in
                    Turkish territory.</p>
                <p>You will please bring the matter to the attention of the government, urging upon
                    it the use of effective means for the protection of Armenians from violence at
                    the hands of those of other religions.</p>
                <p>The Russian Ambassador calls attention to the fact that there are many Mussulmans
                    in Russian territory and that these enjoy immunity from religious
                    persecution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
